  // No type assertion is written (Benjamin, 2026-11-22: "type assertions are banned"): `x as T` and `<T>x` tell the
  // compiler what a value is instead of showing it, and a wrong one reaches the person as a value of the wrong shape.
  // Decode it through a Schema, narrow it with a guard, or annotate it (`const x: T = value`, `value satisfies T`).
  // `as const` says nothing new about a value and stays allowed (measured on oxlint 1.93.0).
